 ],
 "observations": "In this run we observed the agent work in one growing file, appctl.py, adding each feature as a new labelled section built in a /tmp file and spliced in by a Python string-replace script (ck4 step 9, ck5 step 7, ck6 step 19, ck7 steps 16-18). From ck3 on, each session began by grepping the def/class list and then reading wide sed ranges (ck3 step 2, ck4 steps 2-3, ck6 steps 2-3, ck8 steps 2-4); ck2 instead read the whole file with cat (ck2 step 2). In ck1 the agent stated it invented the command set (ck1 step 8 SAY), and later failures trace to those invented commands: sample-data site list never calls docker (ck4, ck6) and site create never creates volumes or networks even though helpers existed (ck6 step 19). Checking was manual throughout: scratch scripts, fake docker or ssh binaries, and CLI runs in temp dirs (ck2 step 18, ck6 step 21, ck7 step 20, ck8 step 24); no test files were added (ck4 SAY). Regression checks against a saved original copy appear in ck2 step 22 and ck8 step 35, but ck8's new docker requirement check and first-run message still broke 31 earlier tests in an environment without docker. Placement errors were found by running: a NameError forced moving the ck4 section above build_registry (ck4 steps 11-12), and a YAML traceback led to editing the parser (ck6 steps 14-17)."
}